---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <Nav />

  <div class="wrap page-wrap">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="updated">Effective August 2026</div>

    <h2>1. What this policy covers</h2>
    <p>This policy explains what data Conchquest collects, why, and how it's used, when you use our mobile app or website.</p>

    <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Why we collect it</th></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Account info</strong> (email, display name)</td><td>To create and secure your account, via our authentication provider. Social login (Google/Apple) shares only what those providers permit.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Precise location</strong> (GPS)</td><td>To fetch tide, weather, and wave conditions for your current beach, and to let you log a find with coordinates.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Photos</strong></td><td>To attach images to shell finds you choose to log, stored with our cloud storage provider.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Find data</strong> (species, condition, notes, timestamp)</td><td>To build your personal shelling history and, if you choose to share it, contribute to the community find map.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Device and usage data</strong></td><td>To keep the app secure, diagnose crashes, and understand feature usage.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Subscription status</strong> (once premium features launch)</td><td>Will be handled by Apple, Google, and RevenueCat to manage premium entitlements. We will not receive or store your payment card details.</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>3. Location privacy controls</h2>
    <p>You control how your location is shared:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Private (default):</strong> your exact find location is visible only to you.</li>
      <li><strong>Approximate:</strong> a fuzzed, general area is shown to the community — never your exact coordinates.</li>
      <li><strong>Rare-find protection:</strong> finds tagged as rare species get additional location fuzzing to discourage over-collection of sensitive sites.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How we use your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To generate your personal Shelling Score and forecasts</li>
      <li>To generate the natural-language "Shelling Strategy" summary for your forecast, via a third-party AI text-generation provider</li>
      <li>To operate the community find map and social features you opt into</li>
      <li>To send you notifications you've enabled (e.g., score-threshold alerts)</li>
      <li>To improve the accuracy of the Shelling Score using aggregated, anonymized community data</li>
      <li>To process subscription billing through Apple/Google and RevenueCat, once premium features launch</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Categories of third parties we work with</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Authentication provider</td><td>Creates and secures your account</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cloud hosting &amp; storage provider</td><td>Runs our backend, database, and stores your uploaded photos</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Environmental data providers</td><td>Tide, weather, and wave forecast data (we send them a location, not your identity)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>AI text-generation provider</td><td>Generates the "Shelling Strategy" natural-language summary from your forecast conditions</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Push notification provider</td><td>Delivers the notifications you've enabled</td></tr>
      <tr><td>RevenueCat, Apple App Store, Google Play</td><td>Subscription billing (once premium features launch — not yet active)</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p class="hint-note">We name Apple, Google, and RevenueCat specifically above since you'll interact with them directly for billing; other categories are handled through providers we may change from time to time.</p>
    <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>

    <h2>6. Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Turn off location access at any time in your device settings (the Shelling Score will no longer auto-detect your beach)</li>
      <li>Delete individual finds or your entire account from Settings</li>
      <li>Request a copy or deletion of your data by contacting us below</li>
      <li>Opt out of push notifications at any time</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
    <p>We keep your account and find data until you delete your account. Deleted finds are removed from the community map immediately; backups are purged within 30 days.</p>

    <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>Conchquest is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we make material changes to how we handle your data, we'll notify you in-app before the changes take effect.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions, or want to exercise a data right? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@conchquest.app">privacy@conchquest.app</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-wrap {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 56px 32px 100px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #9b9a92;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  p,
  li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #3c3c39;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 8px 0 8px;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .hint-note {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #9b9a92;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--teal-deep);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 16px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  th {
    color: #9b9a92;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
</style>
